        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Carraig Bhan, Three Mile Water, County Wicklow.\r\n\r\nA Charming Period Cottage Nestled in Mature Gardens Close to Brittas Bay.\r\n\r\nMcDonnell Properties are delighted to present Charraig Bhán, a truly special cottage residence located in the peaceful countryside setting of Three Mile Water, County Wicklow, only a few kilometres from the stunning coastline of Brittas Bay Beach.\r\nSet behind mature hedging and approached via a charming avenue entrance, Charraig Bhán offers something increasingly rare  a home filled with warmth, nostalgia, and timeless character. This inviting cottage captures the feeling of a simpler time, where original charm, mature gardens, and peaceful surroundings combine to create a wonderfully comforting home.\r\nSurrounded by beautifully established gardens and offering excellent privacy, the property provides an idyllic retreat while remaining conveniently close to local amenities and one of Wicklow’s most treasured beaches.\r\n\r\nAccommodation\r\nUpon arrival, a stepped entrance and gated approach lead you to the front door where a welcoming entrance hallway (approximately 4ft x 3ft) introduces the home’s distinctive character and period atmosphere.\r\n\r\nLiving Room – 12ft 10in x 13ft\r\nThe living room immediately sets the tone for the property. Rich in charm and filled with character, this inviting space features two timber-framed windows allowing natural light to fill the room while maintaining its cosy atmosphere.\r\nAn open fireplace creates a beautiful focal point, enhancing the warmth and comforting feel of the space. The room perfectly captures the cottage’s nostalgic appeal, offering a sense of stepping back to a more peaceful era.\r\nA wonderful feature throughout the property is the impressive vaulted ceilings, adding a surprising sense of space and individuality to the home. Carpet flooring continues throughout much of the cottage, further contributing to its warm and homely feel.\r\n\r\nBedroom One – 10ft x 9ft 2in\r\nA generously proportioned double bedroom featuring vaulted ceilings and a large timber-framed window that floods the room with natural light.\r\n Offering useful storage space. Full of character, it continues the cottage’s charming retro atmosphere.\r\n\r\nBedroom Two – 9ft x 8ft\r\nAnother comfortable bedroom suitable for a child’s room, guest accommodation, or home office. Natural light enters through the window, creating a bright and welcoming space.\r\n\r\nBedroom Three (Principal Bedroom) – 9ft x 8ft\r\nThe principal bedroom continues the home’s warm and inviting style. Benefiting from built-in wardrobes, this room also enjoys the rare addition of an open fireplace, creating a wonderfully cosy and traditional atmosphere.\r\nNatural light from the window enhances the room’s comfortable and peaceful feel.\r\n\r\nKitchen / Dining Area – Approx. 7ft x 11ft\r\nAccessed from the main hallway, the kitchen and dining area continues the cottage’s charming period aesthetic.\r\nQuaint, practical, and full of personality, this space offer linoleum flooring and retains the home’s unique character while providing a welcoming area for everyday living.\r\n\r\nBathroom – Approx. 10ft x 6ft\r\nLocated just off the kitchen, the bathroom is fitted with a bath.\r\nUtility / Larder & Rear Hall\r\nTo the rear of the property is a practical back hallway (approximately 3ft x 3ft) together with a traditional larder space, currently utilised as a laundry area, offering additional functionality and storage.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nOutside Space & Gardens\r\nThe grounds at Charraig Bhán are a true highlight and clearly reflect years of care and passion for gardening.\r\nBeautiful mature trees frame the property while established planting beds, colourful shrubs, hedging for privacy, and generous lawn areas create a peaceful and picturesque setting.\r\nGarden enthusiasts will particularly appreciate the inclusion of a greenhouse, ideal for growing vegetables, flowers, or enjoying year-round gardening.\r\nA pebble-stone driveway and courtyard area provide further charm, complemented by additional planting areas and outdoor spaces to enjoy throughout the seasons.\r\nThe avenue-style driveway offers vehicle access while the front stepped pathway and gated entrance create an attractive approach to the home.\r\n\r\nAdditional Accommodation / Storage\r\nA substantial flat-roof extension measuring approximately 22ft x 16ft provides excellent versatility and potential.\r\nIdeal as a workshop, storage area, hobby space, or vehicle accommodation, this valuable addition offers endless possibilities.\r\nAttached is a further stone outbuilding / shed (approximately 14ft x 8ft) requiring some restoration works but presenting further storage or future-use opportunities."
      },
